# AlignEd web app environment variables.
#
# Copy this file to .env.local and fill in the values. .env.local is
# gitignored, so real secrets never leave your machine. Next.js reads it at
# boot, so restart the dev server after any change.
#
# NEXT_PUBLIC_ values are inlined into the browser bundle and are public.
# Everything else is server-only; never prefix a secret with NEXT_PUBLIC_.

# --- Saved results + admin page (server-only) ------------------------------
# Supabase is only ever reached from route handlers and server components,
# so neither of these is prefixed NEXT_PUBLIC_ and the browser is given
# no Supabase credentials at all.
#
# The project URL and the service_role key, both from Project Settings >
# API. The key bypasses RLS. Either one blank = results are not saved and
# the compare panel stays hidden. Run
# supabase/migrations/0003_saved_results.sql on the project first.
SUPABASE_URL=
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=
# The admin page lives at /admin/<ADMIN_TOKEN>; the link is the only key.
# Use 32+ random characters, e.g.
#   node -e "console.log(require('crypto').randomBytes(24).toString('base64url'))"
# Blank or shorter than 32 = the admin page is off (404). Change it to revoke.
ADMIN_TOKEN=

# --- Email my results (required for POST /api/send-results) ---------------
# The Gmail account that sends the results PDF, and a 16-letter Google App
# Password for it (myaccount.google.com/apppasswords, needs 2FA on the
# account). This is NOT the normal Gmail password. Leave both blank and the
# route returns "not_configured" and the UI tells students to download instead.
GMAIL_USER=
GMAIL_APP_PASSWORD=

# --- PostHog analytics (optional: a no-op when the key is blank) ----------
# Host defaults to https://us.i.posthog.com when unset.
NEXT_PUBLIC_POSTHOG_KEY=
NEXT_PUBLIC_POSTHOG_HOST=
